# Registry profile every end-to-end lane layers over its registries' own:
# ACTIVE_PROFILES=<registry>,payments-lane. The full local stack never loads it.
#
# It recommends the one dispute authority the lanes run, the mediation lane
# double, restating the identity, params and advertisement of
# tools/mediation-lane-double/fixtures/authority.toml as a one-item JSON array,
# single-quoted so the registry's dotenv reader takes it literally; a repository
# test holds the two equal. A public development value, never for a public
# network: its origin is a service name that resolves only where a lane runs the
# double, and its record key derives from a committed seed.
# Sellers use registry recommendations by default and the lanes' buyer profile
# opts in, so no storefront or buyer configuration names a [[Dispute]] entry.
REGISTRY_DESCRIPTOR_RECOMMENDED_DISPUTE_AUTHORITIES='[{"account":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000d1","advertisement":{"mechanisms":["arkhai.payments.v1"],"minimum_dispute_window_seconds":0},"interface":"arkhai.mediation.v1","origin":"https://mediation-double:8443","params":{},"record_key":"ed25519:2b8hSHSKhcidparY7gsPwtEF_TnUGkx5ZTY1TwrikAw"}]'
